From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: features the Amiga browser switches off are not
 built

OpenBrowser switches these Web platform features off at run time (by
setting, or they have no backend in a single-process port), but WebCore
built all of them into the engine, and on the Amiga's linker every
compiled function stays in the program. Each gets a feature flag, on by
default as before, and the Amiga port turns them off:

- ENABLE_ACCESSIBILITY, ENABLE_ASYNC_CLIPBOARD, ENABLE_CACHE_API,
  ENABLE_CREDENTIAL_MANAGEMENT, ENABLE_FILE_SYSTEM_API,
  ENABLE_INDEXED_DATABASE, ENABLE_PUSH_API, ENABLE_SERVICE_WORKER and
  ENABLE_SHARED_WORKER (WebKitFeatures.cmake and PlatformEnable.h,
  default on; OptionsAmiga.cmake sets them off).
- PlatformAmiga.cmake leaves each feature's IDL files, the bindings
  generated from them and its sources out of the build. The bindings
  generator still reads the IDL files (INCLUDED_FILES), so kept IDL files
  may name their types in members that are compiled out. The value types
  that loaders and workers carry stay (ServiceWorkerData and friends,
  CacheStorageConnection, FileSystemStorageConnection).
- Everything else that called into them is compiled out with the flag:
  a document, page or frame view has no accessibility object cache
  (inline null accessors, so the calls behind them compile away), no
  IndexedDB connection, no service worker connection, container or
  controlling service worker; workers have no IndexedDB, cache storage,
  file system or service worker connection; MessageEvent.source cannot
  be a ServiceWorker; DataTransferItem has no webkitGetAsEntry() and
  StorageManager no getDirectory(); structured clone has no file system
  handles. The checks for a service worker or shared worker global scope
  (dynamic import, worker loads, permissions, the worker run loop) are
  under their flags.
- The EventTarget and Event factories list the dropped interfaces under
  their flags, and so do the headers that are still compiled: their type
  casts (SPECIALIZE_TYPE_TRAITS) and the interface types they return
  (EventTargetInterfaceType::Invalid, EventInterfaceType::Invalid when the
  flag is off). JSWorkerGlobalScopeBase.h includes WorkerGlobalScope.h,
  not ServiceWorkerGlobalScope.h.
- Bindings: FileSystemWritableFileStream.idl is Conditional=FILE_SYSTEM_API,
  DOMURL's createObjectURL() and revokeObjectURL() name SharedWorker among
  their globals only when ENABLE_SHARED_WORKER is defined, and
  CodeGeneratorJS.pm puts a child interface's includes under its
  Conditional, as it already did for the code that uses them.
- Stubs for what code outside the dropped folders still names but never
  reaches: accessibility/amiga/AccessibilityDisabledAmiga.cpp answers the
  two accessibility helpers that editing and quirks code call, and has
  empty AccessibilityReplacedText and
  AXObjectCache::handlePageEditibilityChanged() bodies;
  Modules/indexeddb/amiga/IndexedDBDisabledAmiga.cpp has
  IDBConnectionProxy::deref() (never reached: no proxy is made) and
  IDBDatabaseNameAndVersionRequest's two virtual functions.
- Leftovers of features that were already off: GeolocationCoordinates.cpp
  builds only with ENABLE(GEOLOCATION), the supplement type checks of
  dropped features only with their flags, and the empty WebTransport
  session (EmptyClients) only with ENABLE(WEB_TRANSPORT).

Pages see one change: DataTransferItem.webkitGetAsEntry() is gone (the
port has no drag and drop, so it only applied to pasted files). The rest
was already absent or switched off by setting.

